  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-950">Pakistan tour packages: which one to choose</h2>
  <p>Our tours cover the valleys of Gilgit-Baltistan by road, with hotels, a vehicle and driver and a local guide. They are written for travellers from abroad and run on private dates for couples, families and small groups.</p>
  <p><strong>Hunza.</strong> The <a href="/tours/hunza-valley-heritage-tour/">Hunza valley tour</a> covers Baltit and Altit forts, Attabad Lake and the upper valley in ten days. In spring the <a href="/tours/spring-blossom-tour/">Hunza blossom tour</a> follows the apricot and cherry blossom.</p>
  <p><strong>Skardu.</strong> The <a href="/tours/skardu-shigar-valley-explorer/">Skardu and Shigar valley tour</a> takes seven days for the lakes, the cold deserts and Shigar fort. The <a href="/tours/deosai-khaplu-tour/">Deosai and Khaplu tour</a> adds the high plateau.</p>
  <p><strong>Both valleys.</strong> The <a href="/tours/gilgit-baltistan-grand-circuit/">Gilgit-Baltistan Grand Circuit</a> links Hunza and Skardu in fourteen days, and the <a href="/tours/autumn-hunza-skardu-tour/">autumn tour</a> does the same for the October colour. <a href="/tours/fairy-meadows-nanga-parbat-tour/">Fairy Meadows</a> adds Nanga Parbat.</p>
  <p><strong>When to go.</strong> Late March to mid-April for blossom, May to September for open roads, and mid-October to early November for autumn colour. See our <a href="/destinations/hunza/">Hunza</a> and <a href="/destinations/skardu/">Skardu</a> travel guides.</p>
